  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>fremanezumab</td></tr><tr><td>ATC code:</td><td>N02CD03</td></tr><tr><td>model:</td><td>two compartments, oral dosing <small>(PK_2C_enteral)</small></td></tr><tr><td>source:</td><td>Jones A et al. 2021</td></tr><tr><td>population:</td><td>pediatric patients with migraine</td></tr><tr><td>measured compound:</td><td>fremanezumab</td></tr><tr><td>review:</td><td>accepted with caveats</td></tr><tr><td>record page:</td><td><a href=\"https://pharmacolibrary.github.io/#/drugs/drug_fremanezumab/Fremanezumab_Jones2021_previously_developed_adult_model_appl\">pharmacolibrary-docs</a></td></tr></table><h4>Parameters as reported in the paper</h4><table border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=2><tr><th>parameter</th><th>value</th><th>unit</th><th>meaning</th></tr><tr><td>CL: central clearance (L/day)</td><td>0.0902</td><td>L/day</td><td><small>CL</small></td></tr><tr><td>Vc: central volume of distribution (L)</td><td>1.88</td><td>L</td><td><small>V1</small></td></tr><tr><td>ka: absorption rate constant (1/day)</td><td>0.180</td><td>1/day</td><td><small>kabs</small></td></tr><tr><td>Q: intercompartmental clearance (L/day)</td><td>0.262</td><td>L/day</td><td><small>Q</small></td></tr><tr><td>Vp: peripheral volume of distribution (L)</td><td>1.72</td><td>L</td><td><small>V2</small></td></tr><tr><td>ALAG1: lag time (day)</td><td>0.0803</td><td>day</td><td><small>tlag</small></td></tr><tr><td>theta_q319_weight_power</td><td>1.05</td><td></td><td><small>equation variable</small></td></tr><tr><td>theta_q319_weight_power</td><td>1.53</td><td></td><td><small>equation variable</small></td></tr></table><h4>About fremanezumab</h4><p>Fremanezumab is a monoclonal antibody used to prevent migraine, including migraine with and without aura. It is an approved CGRP-antagonist medicine authorised in the European Union for migraine prevention.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q39048381\">Wikidata Q39048381</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Fremanezumab\">Fremanezumab</a>.</p><h4>References</h4><ol><li><p>Jones A et al. (2021). Scaling Approaches for Pediatric Dose Selection: The Fremanezumab (AJOVY. <i>Pharmaceutics 13(6)</i>. DOI:<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.3390/pharmaceutics13060785\">10.3390/pharmaceutics13060785</a> PUBMED:<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34074002\">34074002</a></p></li></ol></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Jones_2021: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: accepted with caveats</li></ul></body></html>"),
